{
	"name": "Mistmander",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/lizard-mouth-glowing-red.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>These Tiny salamanders are bright reddish- orange with striking black blotches that emit a faint mist of steam off of their sleek skin. When threatened, startled, or if water is poured onto them, a mistmander will rapidly increase its internal body temperature, emitting a cloud of warm steam. Creatures who are within 10 feet of a mistmander gain the benefits of being lightly obscured for 1 minute or until they exit the cloud.</p><p>In urban locales, saunas often have mistmanders on-hand to help assist with producing steam and maintaining the proper temperature. They require higher than average ambient temperatures and a steady diet of warm coals to maintain their body heat. If a mistmander’s body temperature dips too low, they inevitably die.</p>",
